{"kind":"request","text":"Design review, Draft 4: durability level declared by each scope, and the journal archive in Git. notes/2026-10-09-shared-language-volatile-acts.md at head 6d0ce3c7 (branch planner/journal-archive-design; parent b2ab1e55, Draft 3, merged with main 70729eac; request 0d72a50b, promise fae322e0). Reporting artifact: the note. Draft 4 answers each point of report 7e549a27. P1, 16.2: the live seed's cause is the digest of the establishing act's signed intent, as Seed.cause is for every native seed, with the ordinal for which live scope of that intent; the seed is built before the entry is sealed and the entry records the derived ID, so nothing in the seed depends on the entry's hash; a bounded locator {host, established, ordinal} travels with discovery and each request, and the object rebuilds the seed from the host's sealed entry and accepts only its own name; the identity witness constructs the real intent, entry and seed on a real host and starts from no prebuilt ID. P2, 15.6 and A4: followArchived binds the full ScopeRef, incarnation included, and confirms a receipt at its own position: n past through waits, n at or below it is checked against the service's entry n under the same incarnation by the chain, another incarnation is not-this-history, a differing hash is mismatch, no archive is not-archived, a stopped or conflicting archive reports its state; through is stated to be the last read-back, not a fresh remote read, and a moved ref surfaces at the next pass as conflict; the clone-side check, artroom-replay --git --receipt, is the only one that does not trust the service; A4 lists every case. P2, 15.3 and 15.5: the input set of a pass is closed under the cutoff, the retained inputs exactly those the archived entries name, omissions (text, J2 domains) listed by kind, domain and digest; the Mark row persists the manifest's bytes with the parent, cutoff and commit ID, a restart or resend rebuilds from the row never from current storage, a rebuild that differs stops as rebuild-mismatch; the commit is a function of parent, cutoff, object format and manifest; A3 witnesses a parent still unupdated, a new input retained after Mark, and the identical commit resent after a restart. P2, 15.4 and A1/A2: the ref is refs/artroom/journal/\u003csc_ plus 52 base32\u003e, the native spelling, no conversion; every path segment is from [a-z0-9_.-], a digest is its 64 hex characters, a byte domain is d_ plus the base32 of its UTF-8 bytes, decoded and compared by the verifier; the Git source resolves commit, tree and blobs through the object store by ID, refuses symlinks, submodules and out-of-grammar segments, never joins a clone path to a filesystem path; A1 round-trips every platform domain and adversarial names. P2, 16.3/16.4/L5: the section 11 row withdraws the absolute claim; a live object's reads of its host are bounded per generation, per second and in flight and refused busy past the bound, the host refuses busy rather than queueing, an act needing no read is not throttled; 16.5 adds a mixed host-read and flood witness with the measured budget recorded; L5 carries the bound into sections 5 and 9; L6 names where the locator travels. Unchanged: one pinned level per scope, zero-durability live, explicit promotion, the asynchronous archive, no migration, register and inbox excluded, J2 screening before export. Design only; no runtime adoption, no tests, gate or probes. Exact-head review with the three conclusions.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a7906ea9a64d92c1194786dca615ddccd1bee20e","branch":"planner/journal-archive-design","conditions":"Independent exact-head review of 6d0ce3c7…8d69b62 with explicit Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions, filed with gs review naming git:sha1…1bee20e first and resting on all 1 artifacts.","head":"6d0ce3c72eb8ac90e226eed4bbe231f2b8d69b62","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22f